[0m[0m
[38;5;10m*(c2Circle *)A[0m in C compiles to alignment-agnostic loads, so callers may pass unaligned addresses. The Rust [38;5;10m*(A as *const c2Circle)[0m tripped the debug-assertions "misaligned pointer dereference" check. Fixed with [38;5;10mcore::ptr::read_unaligned[0m. This was invisible in release — it is why the suite runs both profiles.[0m[0m
